.TH "YAMLR-FOUNDER" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-founder \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBStrategic Command Center\fR
.PP
The \fBfounder\fR command is a privileged operational dashboard designed for the Yamlr project founder to monitor ecosystem health and strategic metrics.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr founder [ACTION]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Aggregates global telemetry (anonymized) to provide a macro-view of product performance, rule efficacy, and user friction points.
.PP
.SH "ACTIONS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fBdashboard\fR\fR: (Default) Show high-level strategic KPI dashboard.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fBerrors\fR\fR: View the latest anonymized fatal exception reports from the community.
.SH "OUTPUT"
Displays real-time metrics including:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Global ROI (Wealth Reclaimed)
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Rule Heatmap (Most frequently triggered rules)
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Top 10 failing K8s clusters (by version)
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Infrastructure health of the license server
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
yamlr founder dashboard
.RE
.fi
.SH "PRIVACY & SECURITY"
This command only displays data that has been explicitly anonymized and uploaded via the telemetry layer. No raw YAML data or PII is ever visible in the founder dashboard.
.PP
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
